Q: QT QML How to chain QAbstractListModel and QSortFilterProxyModel A: <p>For version 1, of your app, I would look at either <a href="https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/qvariant.html#QVariantList-typedef" rel="nofollow noreferrer">QVariantList</a> from the C++ side or <a href="https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/qml-list.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>list&lt;var&gt;</code></a> from the QML side. Using these two will mean you don't need to worry about QSortFilterProxyModel. The Javascript <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array/filter" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Array.prototype.filter()</a>, <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array/sort" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Array.prototype.sort()</a> and <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array/slice" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Array.prototype.slice()</a> will work directly on <code>list&lt;var&gt;</code>. For example:</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>// Wrap the parsed dataSet in a `list&lt;var&gt;` type
property list&lt;var&gt; dataSet: JSON.parse(dataSets[currentSet])
property int limit: 2

// Demonstration of
//  - 1. filter on arbitrary condition (e.g. &gt;= &quot;3&quot;)
//  - 2. sort (e.g. sort on name descending)
//  - 3. slice (e.g. to 2 results)
ListView {
    anchors.fill: parent
    model: dataSet
               .filter(d =&gt; d.id &gt;= &quot;3&quot;)
               .sort((a,b) =&gt; -a.name.localeCompare(b.name))
               .slice(0,limit)
    delegate: Label { text: JSON.stringify(modelData) }
}
</code></pre>
<p>You can <a href="https://stephenquan.github.io/qmlonline/?" rel="nofollow noreferrer">demo the above code online</a>.</p>
